   {
    "author": "marcelometal",
    "date": "2026-08-27",
    "bot": false,
    "body": "Thanks for the detailed report and the useful format matrix. I reproduced the\nfailure on current `master` and opened #1887 with a fix.\n\nThe issue is in the indexed-mode path you identified. After resizing, Thumbor\nquantizes the RGBA image back to `P`; the resulting palette still contains its\nalpha values, but Pillow does not set `image.info[\"transparency\"]`. PNG can\nencode the palette alpha directly, while the GIF writer receives an already\nindexed image and therefore does not infer the single transparent index.\n\n#1887 restores that index from the fully transparent palette entry before GIF\nencoding and adds a regression test using the binary-alpha palette source from\nthis issue. With the default `PILLOW_PRESERVE_INDEXED_MODE = True`, the output\nnow retains `info[\"transparency\"] == 1` and the same 4,800 transparent pixels as\nthe working non-preserving path. The full CI matrix is green.\n\nCould you please test #1887 with your integration setup and confirm that it\nresolves the issue there as well?"
   },
